msgid "**Pause/Resume Search** - The pause means that it will stop the background search, but you can still view its results"
msgstr ""

#: ../userguides/imagery_search.rst:242
#: 027f865cac1d4b6bafa4323b87609f99
msgid "**Delete** - Permanently deletes the search"
msgstr ""

#: ../userguides/imagery_search.rst:245
#: 13db29dbfc734ed980dc25a12e5886a3
msgid "Modifying the AOI search"
msgstr ""

#: ../userguides/imagery_search.rst:247
#: 8f28b2bb414e4c5a90f097e71a5c95ef
msgid "You can add a new AOI to an existing search, modify the geometry, or delete areas that have already been processed. After any AOI changes, you will need to confirm these changes. The search will be updated, and the **results will be synchronized** accordingly."
msgstr ""

#: ../userguides/imagery_search.rst:None
#: 1129b4c0b5684bc8a76ad6840167c6ae
msgid "Update template"
msgstr ""

#: ../userguides/imagery_search.rst:257
#: c241052cce9143acbd4e7bab5949593b
msgid "**You can also change the search criteria for the existing search:**"
msgstr ""

#: ../userguides/imagery_search.rst:259
#: fee1c66e693d498dbd306bad3ad65265
msgid "\"View on the map\" → Adjust the search parameters → \"Search Imagery\" → \"Save as schedule\". Now the background search will work according to the new parameters."
msgstr ""

#: ../userguides/imagery_search.rst:270
#: 5016daaf7f6540eb82459eadf8d3791a
msgid "Using Mapflow Imagery Search in QGIS"
msgstr ""

#: ../userguides/imagery_search.rst:272
#: e33d3b38b74b4f9d8df1985995135c30
msgid "Switch to the tab \"Imagery Search\". To start the search, set the dates and the product type filters (\"Mosaic\" – Imagery basemaps like ArcGIS or Global mosaic and/or \"Images\" - Satellite imagery archives)"
msgstr ""

#: ../userguides/imagery_search.rst:273
#: 578e2406f0a0468d8b8719eb35aa0d97
msgid "Set additional filters like a minimum intersection with your area of analysis."
msgstr ""

#: ../userguides/imagery_search.rst:274
#: d545fe160c454c7bb1e23e39ee55f645
msgid "If there is non-empty response, it will add the **🔎 Imagery Search metadata** layer to your QGIS project. You can select one or multiple results in the table - or use the layer's attribute table to start the analysis and processing with Mapflow models."
msgstr ""

#: ../userguides/imagery_search.rst:283
#: 79d1bd3f7bca4a5689b2fa0d89eaac35
msgid "In the Arcgis search results you see the zoom level at which the mosaic is available over you area. You can configure the table columns in the Settings."
msgstr ""

#: ../userguides/imagery_search.rst:293
#: d667cb236f6e4bf88e7b45915d97406b
msgid "👉 See :ref:`Mapflow <> QGIS` for more information on how to use Imagery Search in Mapflow Web and QGIS plugin."
msgstr ""

#: ../userguides/imagery_search.rst:296
#: 5016daaf7f6540eb82459eadf8d3791a
msgid "Planned Search in QGIS"
msgstr ""

#: ../userguides/imagery_search.rst:298
#: 0f8721b25ce5453fb11e95c94944900b
msgid "**Planned Search** is a recurring background search. You define the search area and parameters once, and Mapflow keeps looking for new imagery over that area - you will be notified when new images are found. The search runs in the background, so you can keep working with the plugin in the meantime, review the results at any time and start processing directly from them."
msgstr ""

#: ../userguides/imagery_search.rst:301
#: a7655735eea54290ba8741f938b9313a
msgid "Creating a planned search"
msgstr ""

#: ../userguides/imagery_search.rst:303
#: 97aecbe26fe04f2f8d23ae030485f0e8
msgid "Switch to the **Imagery Search** tab and set the area of interest: draw it on the map or select an existing polygon layer (for example, a GeoJSON file loaded into QGIS). If the layer has a ``name`` attribute, it will be used as the AOI name. AOI names can also be assigned or changed later."
msgstr ""

#: ../userguides/imagery_search.rst:304
#: ecfd91dd77854911ba4aa082e50600eb
msgid "Set the search parameters: date range, cloud cover, off-nadir angle, minimum intersection, product types and providers."
msgstr ""

#: ../userguides/imagery_search.rst:305
#: 3271bc28ec34467fa49a47235de818a6
msgid "Specify the search name in the **Processing name** field."
msgstr ""

#: ../userguides/imagery_search.rst:306
#: 9c7f2d438c4047708e75934576eccce1
msgid "Open the **Search** button menu and choose **Plan search**."
msgstr ""

#: ../userguides/imagery_search.rst:315
#: ed53ed37fe0846999a5ce80d6f9ba631
msgid "The planned search is created and starts running in the background. It will keep looking for new imagery over the selected areas, and you will be notified when results are ready."
msgstr ""

#: ../userguides/imagery_search.rst:317
#: 1b9a0940904f4aabb6d1312439c92ec2
msgid "The planned search appears in the **Processing** table with the workflow **\"Planned\"**. Its status reflects the search state:"
msgstr ""

#: ../userguides/imagery_search.rst:319
#: a0b705005da440e581eda799d1ce8c76
msgid "**Searching** – the initial search is in progress;"
msgstr ""

#: ../userguides/imagery_search.rst:320
#: da384e306ff64a8f9dca58c9b9ae93bb
msgid "**Created / Updated** – the search is active and being checked for new imagery (the number of new images, e.g. *Updated (3)*, is shown when there are any);"
msgstr ""

#: ../userguides/imagery_search.rst:321
#: b12582c0ead141a6b6a2bd0e3d94a916
msgid "**Inactive** – the search is paused;"
msgstr ""

#: ../userguides/imagery_search.rst:322
#: c241052cce9143acbd4e7bab5949593b
msgid "**Failed** – the search failed and can be restarted."
msgstr ""

#: ../userguides/imagery_search.rst:332
#: d13eac99c5554efa80e8b9b66239e780
msgid "If the area of interest is too large for an immediate search, clicking **Search** will prompt you to create a planned search instead - the search area would take too long to process synchronously. Confirm with **Plan Search**, and the planned search will be created and run in the background."
msgstr ""

#: ../userguides/imagery_search.rst:340
#: 048497593f9242ec93e0d03b69b30845
msgid "Opening a planned search"
msgstr ""

#: ../userguides/imagery_search.rst:342
#: ../userguides/imagery_search.rst:342
#: 59fe78898aea438296420651e55dc014
#: 59fe78898aea438296420651e55dc014
msgid "right_arrow"
msgstr ""

#: ../userguides/imagery_search.rst:346
#: 51cba05af2f6483e8faa78265b1364bb
msgid "Select the planned search in the **Processing** table and click the |right_arrow| navigation button (or double-click the row). The plugin enters the planned search view: the table now shows the search AOIs, each followed by the processings that were launched for it, and the **\"No AOI\"** group for processings not linked to any area."
msgstr ""

#: ../userguides/imagery_search.rst:355
#: e74a0dc8803d4be489e3b9dbb7a60d57
msgid "The AOI rows show the aggregate status of their processings (*OK (n)*, *In progress*, *Failed*). On the map, the planned search is displayed in a dedicated group in the Layers panel — each AOI and its processings are grouped together, and processings not tied to any AOI appear on the map when you click them."
msgstr ""

#: ../userguides/imagery_search.rst:365
#: 5b7067060b374468af94f4aafb452cf2
msgid "Viewing the search results"
msgstr ""

#: ../userguides/imagery_search.rst:367
#: 4e39e415ab69401fbaf5fadca48f219e
msgid "Open the planned search and switch to the **Imagery Search** tab. The table shows the images found for **all** AOIs of the planned search. To display results only for specific areas, select the corresponding AOI rows in the processings table - the results are updated automatically."
msgstr ""

#: ../userguides/imagery_search.rst:369
#: e5323e07a4c14850b910656d425e2173
msgid "New images are marked with the **(!)** sign. You can mark the selected new images as seen with the **Seen** button, or mark all of them with **Seen all** - the label will disappear."
msgstr ""

#: ../userguides/imagery_search.rst:378
#: 58498a85e7a442fa8a048be7f0bc6e71
msgid "You can also adjust the search criteria of the existing planned search: change the filters (dates, cloud cover, off-nadir angle, intersection, providers) on the **Imagery Search** tab and click **Update search** — the new parameters are saved to the planned search, and the results are re-fetched with them. The results can be sorted by clicking the column headers."
msgstr ""

#: ../userguides/imagery_search.rst:381
#: 97e64de9a1604c1bab82ff4cdc29ad26
msgid "Running processing from the search results"
msgstr ""

#: ../userguides/imagery_search.rst:383
#: 8bc4328d09904637900be471755fb4da
msgid "Select one or several images in the results table and click **Start planned processing** - the processing will be launched from the selected imagery, linked to this planned search. The new processing appears in the processings table grouped under the AOI it intersects, and its footprint is displayed on the map."
msgstr ""

#: ../userguides/imagery_search.rst:393
#: 13db29dbfc734ed980dc25a12e5886a3
msgid "Managing the search AOIs"
msgstr ""

#: ../userguides/imagery_search.rst:395
#: 60ab53ab77d04c2ba1277c046a569241
msgid "Select an AOI row and open the options menu (the \"...\" button next to *View results*):"
msgstr ""

#: ../userguides/imagery_search.rst:397
#: 97e64de9a1604c1bab82ff4cdc29ad26
msgid "**Rename AOI** – assign a new name to the area;"
msgstr ""

#: ../userguides/imagery_search.rst:398
#: 027f865cac1d4b6bafa4323b87609f99
msgid "**Delete AOI** – remove the area from the search;"
msgstr ""

#: ../userguides/imagery_search.rst:399
#: 5f59ca4736a9420dbeaf833732b2b3d4
msgid "**Add AOI from layer…** – add new areas from polygon layers in your QGIS project (for example, a GeoJSON file);"
msgstr ""

#: ../userguides/imagery_search.rst:400
#: 68dec667600e402381d73a58414d9358
msgid "**Draw AOI on the map** – draw a new area with the QGIS add-feature tool and save it;"
msgstr ""

#: ../userguides/imagery_search.rst:401
#: 59c14a4ec1d44885a5737c219759b87c
msgid "**Update selected AOI** – edit the geometry of the area right on the map (move the vertices, then click **Save AOI**);"
msgstr ""

#: ../userguides/imagery_search.rst:402
#: d8784bec462b469a98c1870cf5daa7b1
msgid "**Exclude from search** – remove the already processed area from the search AOI (available on a processing row): the footprint of the processing is subtracted from every AOI it intersects, so this area will no longer be searched for new imagery."
msgstr ""

#: ../userguides/imagery_search.rst:411
#: 7879925e123c4696bf7b80d41ed01bfe
msgid "After any AOI change the search is updated, and the search results are synchronized accordingly. Take a look at AOI management in action:"
msgstr ""

#: ../userguides/imagery_search.rst:421
#: b767b93405bc4aa89283913de4ce8850
msgid "**Exclude from search** is a convenient way to gradually free up the search from already processed areas whose search results you no longer need."
msgstr ""

#: ../userguides/imagery_search.rst:429
#: d236e0db6f884eaa8bbe0fa7673b36c0
msgid "Pausing, resuming and restarting a planned search"
msgstr ""

#: ../userguides/imagery_search.rst:431
#: be04eca2113a4f4d85bdaaede47cea00
msgid "Select the planned search in the **Processing** table and open the options menu:"
msgstr ""

#: ../userguides/imagery_search.rst:433
#: c595755416da47fbb652c5d8f648c755
msgid "**Pause** – stops the background search: no more updates on newly found images, but the search results remain available and you can still run processing from them;"
msgstr ""

#: ../userguides/imagery_search.rst:434
#: 4f773cf0b1034054baecedefed7cafcc
msgid "**Resume** – activates the paused search again;"
msgstr ""

#: ../userguides/imagery_search.rst:435
#: a8f9236be2d641959bf590aae1f6740e
msgid "**Restart** – re-runs the search that failed."
msgstr ""

#: ../userguides/imagery_search.rst:445
#: 5b7067060b374468af94f4aafb452cf2
msgid "Planned search limits"
msgstr ""

#: ../userguides/imagery_search.rst:447
#: 62cbd35ea01941ae89c37b0b07fec9b2
msgid "If the search area is too large for an immediate search, you will be prompted to create a planned search automatically (see above)."
msgstr ""

#: ../userguides/imagery_search.rst:448
#: d06022982c734262881d080ceb3644dc
msgid "On the free plan you cannot create a planned search larger than **1000 km²**."
msgstr ""

#: ../userguides/imagery_search.rst:449
#: 8a36589a105a4ebfb406bd4083499bed
msgid "On the free plan you can have up to **2 active** planned searches. If you exceed this limit, new searches can still be created, but they will be added in a **paused** state. Upgrade your plan to resume them and create new active searches."
msgstr ""
